// City 2MC of Maxwell et al. (2014): a 15 x 15 mile city with two demand peaks
// side by side, moderately concentrated, and 25 bases clustered under the
// demand. Seven ambulances answer 3 calls an hour for a day. The demand of
// each 3-mile cell is the mass that the Gaussian peaks of Figure 6 of the
// paper put in it. The home bases (the static policy, which the paper does not
// list) are chosen by maximal expected covering (Daskin 1983). The horizon
// leaves room for the events of a day, about 320 and rarely over 500, and the
// episode ends after the day.

